I might have a possible workaround. I have a chart with points, a line, and two ribbons. When I put the ribbons later in the code they cover the dots a bit (set to 0.1 opacity). This also has the effect of assigning a "0" tooltip to the entire space covered by the ribbons (incidentally the whole chart). Moving the ribbons to the top of my script moves the dots to the fore (like bring to front in PowerPoint) which then shows only tooltips for my dots and none for the ribbons.

